---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../config/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description={`Terms of Use for ${siteConfig.name}. Rules for downloading and playing our lip-reading party game, including subscriptions and acceptable use.`}
  path="/terms"
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: {siteConfig.lastUpdated}</p>
      <div class="legal-content">
        <p>
          These Terms of Use (“Terms”) govern your access to and use of the {siteConfig.name}
          mobile application and website (the “Service”) operated by {siteConfig.legalEntity}
          (“we”, “us”, or “our”). By downloading, accessing, or using the Service, you agree to these
          Terms.
        </p>

        <h2>1. The Service</h2>
        <p>
          {siteConfig.name} is a lip-reading party game you can play locally on one device or online
          with friends. Features may change over time as we improve the product.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Eligibility</h2>
        <p>
          You must be old enough to use the App Store / Google Play in your region and to consent to
          these Terms. If you use the Service on behalf of someone else, you confirm you have
          authority to accept these Terms for them.
        </p>

        <h2>3. License</h2>
        <p>
          We grant you a personal, limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to use
          the app for entertainment, subject to these Terms and the store rules of Apple or Google.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Accounts and rooms</h2>
        <p>
          Online play may require creating or joining a room. You are responsible for how you share
          room codes and for conduct during matches. Do not disrupt sessions, harass other players, or
          attempt to interfere with servers, video sessions, or other users’ devices.
        </p>

        <h2>5. User content and recordings</h2>
        <p>
          You are responsible for phrases you speak, anything visible on camera, and any recordings
          you choose to save. Do not use the Service to share illegal, hateful, sexual content
          involving minors, or otherwise harmful material. You grant us a limited license to process
          live session media solely to operate online play.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Subscriptions and purchases</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Local pass-and-play is available without a paid subscription. Online features may include
            a free allowance and paid upgrades (for example weekly, monthly, or yearly Pro, or round
            packs).
          </li>
          <li>
            Prices are shown in the store at purchase time and may vary by territory.
          </li>
          <li>
            Subscriptions renew automatically unless canceled at least 24 hours before the end of the
            current period through your Apple ID or Google Play account settings.
          </li>
          <li>
            Refunds are handled by Apple or Google under their respective policies.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          For Apple users, Licensed Application End User License Agreement terms also apply:
          <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/"
            >Apple Standard EULA</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Reverse engineer, scrape, or attack the Service except where law allows</li>
          <li>Circumvent paywalls, quotas, or security controls</li>
          <li>Misuse camera/microphone access to harm or secretly record others without consent</li>
          <li>Use the Service for any unlawful purpose</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>8. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The Service, branding, decks, UI, and related materials are owned by us or our licensors.
          These Terms do not transfer ownership to you.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          The Service relies on third parties such as app stores, analytics, crash reporting, live
          video, backend hosting, and purchase validation. Their terms and privacy policies may also
          apply.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>
          The Service is provided “as is” and “as available.” To the fullest extent permitted by law,
          we disclaim warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and
          non-infringement. Party games involve playful social interaction — play responsibly and
          respect everyone in the room (or on the call).
        </p>

        <h2>11. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect, incidental,
          special, consequential, or punitive damages, or any loss of data, profits, or goodwill
          arising from your use of the Service. Our total liability for any claim relating to the
          Service is limited to the greater of (a) the amount you paid us for the Service in the 12
          months before the claim or (b) USD $50.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Termination</h2>
        <p>
          You may stop using the Service at any time. We may suspend or terminate access if you
          violate these Terms or if we discontinue the product.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms. The “Last updated” date will change when we do. Continued use
          after changes become effective constitutes acceptance.
        </p>

        <h2>14. Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by the laws applicable in your primary place of business for
          {siteConfig.legalEntity}, without regard to conflict-of-law rules, except where mandatory
          consumer protections in your country require otherwise.
        </p>

        <h2>15. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these Terms:
          <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}`}>{siteConfig.supportEmail}</a>
        </p>
        <p>
          Related: <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
